From 701cbfff150cf25002a2e3d48e0ad63af452acda Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Andreas Helbech Kleist <andreaskleist@gmail.com>
Date: Sun, 11 Oct 2026 05:21:57 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] media: ipu6: Run IPU4 without iWake

When a stream starts or stops, the driver sends the iWake watermark
settings to the ISYS firmware as proxy tokens (GDA threshold and
enable, as on IPU4P) and updates the buttress LTR/DID values. The IPU4
reference driver does neither: on IPU4 hardware no proxy token is ever
sent and the buttress fabric control register is never written while
streaming. Each proxy token waits up to 100 ms for a response that
IPU4 firmware is not known to send, so the stream start is delayed and
logs "write 2 failed -110" and "write 1 failed -110".

Skip the stream watermark update on IPU4, as is done for IPU7. The
LTR/DID values are already left alone at ISYS suspend on IPU4.

Signed-off-by: Andreas Helbech Kleist <andreaskleist@gmail.com>
---
 drivers/media/pci/intel/ipu6/ipu6-isys-video.c | 3 ++-
 1 file changed, 2 insertions(+), 1 deletion(-)

diff --git a/drivers/media/pci/intel/ipu6/ipu6-isys-video.c b/drivers/media/pci/intel/ipu6/ipu6-isys-video.c
index d9cab5b5d..fcab2285f 100644
--- a/drivers/media/pci/intel/ipu6/ipu6-isys-video.c
+++ b/drivers/media/pci/intel/ipu6/ipu6-isys-video.c
@@ -729,7 +729,8 @@ void ipu6_isys_update_stream_watermark(struct ipu6_isys_video *av, bool state)
 		&av->isys->iwake_watermark;
 	struct ipu6_device *isp = av->isys->adev->isp;
 
-	if (IS_IPU7(isp) ||
+	/* IPU4 runs without iWake: no watermark proxy writes, no LTR/DID. */
+	if (IS_IPU7(isp) || IS_IPU4(isp) ||
 	    !av->watermark.pixel_rate)
 		return;
 
